WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.610
There are so many video
streaming services right now,

00:00:02.610 --> 00:00:05.752
Netflix, Disney+, HBO Max, NBCUniversal,

00:00:05.752 --> 00:00:06.910
blah, blah, blah.

00:00:06.910 --> 00:00:09.980
They just launched the
Peacock streaming service.

00:00:09.980 --> 00:00:12.080
You'd think that's more
than enough, right?

00:00:12.080 --> 00:00:13.650
You'd think that would be all you'd need,

00:00:13.650 --> 00:00:15.290
like we're all done.

00:00:15.290 --> 00:00:16.530
But guess what?

00:00:16.530 --> 00:00:18.800
If you did guess that, you'd be wrong,

00:00:18.800 --> 00:00:22.630
because yet another new
video streaming service

00:00:22.630 --> 00:00:24.910
launched just today.

00:00:24.910 --> 00:00:26.310
That's right.

00:00:26.310 --> 00:00:27.143
Take a look.

00:00:28.290 --> 00:00:29.580
[Andy] In the past four months,

00:00:29.580 --> 00:00:31.690
Zoom has become a way of life.

00:00:31.690 --> 00:00:33.310
And now, that trend continues

00:00:33.310 --> 00:00:37.540
with the latest video streaming
service, Zoom to the Max.

00:00:37.540 --> 00:00:38.690
Thanks to our policy

00:00:38.690 --> 00:00:41.860
of secretly recording every
Zoom meeting ever held,

00:00:41.860 --> 00:00:44.870
Zoom to the Max can now
offer you a streaming library

00:00:44.870 --> 00:00:47.400
of literally millions of videos,

00:00:47.400 --> 00:00:50.850
including such classics as the
co-workers who stay on Zoom

00:00:50.850 --> 00:00:53.160
after a meeting to trash everyone else.

00:00:53.160 --> 00:00:55.190
You guys see that his virtual background

00:00:55.190 --> 00:00:57.440
was his daughter's
Princeton acceptance letter?

00:00:57.440 --> 00:00:58.299
Oh.

00:00:58.299 --> 00:01:00.160
What a (bleep) tool.

00:01:00.160 --> 00:01:01.510
[Raymond] I'm still here.

00:01:03.820 --> 00:01:04.740
Yeah, we knew that.

00:01:04.740 --> 00:01:06.800
[Andy] Obligatory chats with your parents.

00:01:06.800 --> 00:01:10.470
I mean, her father wasn't
in the best of health.

00:01:10.470 --> 00:01:12.010
He was pretty obese.

00:01:12.010 --> 00:01:14.880
I don't know what the family
was eating, but whatever.

00:01:14.880 --> 00:01:16.910
She was pretty chunky-looking, too,

00:01:16.910 --> 00:01:18.800
the other day when I saw her.

00:01:18.800 --> 00:01:21.400
[Andy] Getting on a Zoom
meeting on the wrong day.

00:01:26.100 --> 00:01:26.933
Hey.

00:01:28.950 --> 00:01:29.783
Guys?

00:01:31.500 --> 00:01:33.510
[Andy] The best of poorly-lit meetings.

00:01:33.510 --> 00:01:36.950
And you know that each of you belongs

00:01:36.950 --> 00:01:39.810
to a different team.

00:01:39.810 --> 00:01:41.250
[Andy] Zoom bloopers.

00:01:41.250 --> 00:01:42.760
So we'd probably be better off going

00:01:42.760 --> 00:01:44.660
with a motherboard that has an integrated

00:01:44.660 --> 00:01:46.290
10 gigabit ethernet connection.

00:01:46.290 --> 00:01:47.255
That way, hey!

00:01:47.255 --> 00:01:52.255
(screaming)
(crashing)

00:01:52.550 --> 00:01:53.690
[Andy] Zoom Tinder dates.

00:01:53.690 --> 00:01:55.954
Ah.
Oh my god.

00:01:55.954 --> 00:01:56.830
(dog growling)

00:01:56.830 --> 00:01:58.320
Ah.
Oh!

00:01:58.320 --> 00:01:59.280
Yeah.
(dog growling)

00:01:59.280 --> 00:02:01.020
[Andy] Zoom Bloopers, Volume 2.

00:02:01.020 --> 00:02:02.630
Just for our third quarter goals,

00:02:02.630 --> 00:02:03.463
if we could make sure that-

00:02:03.463 --> 00:02:07.220
(crashing)
(screaming)

00:02:07.220 --> 00:02:08.540
[Andy] And Volume 3.

00:02:08.540 --> 00:02:10.120
So we don't have to worry about wasting

00:02:10.120 --> 00:02:11.188
a lot of time rebuilding volumes

00:02:11.188 --> 00:02:12.021
in the event of a-

00:02:12.021 --> 00:02:15.020
(shouting)

00:02:15.020 --> 00:02:16.510
Oh.

00:02:16.510 --> 00:02:17.343
Oh.

00:02:17.343 --> 00:02:18.551
I'm okay.

00:02:18.551 --> 00:02:21.650
[Andy] Zoom to the Max,
because Quibi lowered the bar.

00:02:21.650 --> 00:02:24.317
(upbeat music)

